Backport of sharp v0.35.4 security fix for GHSA-rgj7-g3m4-5g8c.

The vulnerability is a heap-buffer-overflow in libheif (advisories
GHSA-g89c-p67h-r497 / GHSA-2jg2-4ch7-h545) that sharp consumes through the
bundled libvips. Upstream fixed it in v0.35.4 by bumping the prebuilt native
dependencies rather than changing JS source:

  * @img/sharp-libvips-* 1.3.2 -> 1.3.3 (bundles patched libheif 1.23.2)
  * @img/sharp-* prebuilt binaries 0.35.3 -> 0.35.4
  * config.libvips compile guard >=8.18.3 -> >=8.18.6

This backport applies the security-relevant native-dependency pins onto the
0.35.3 tree (unrelated dev-tooling version bumps from the release are omitted)
and adds a regression test asserting the pinned versions never regress below
the fixed levels.

